---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | ZoneOfWar"
  description="How Siivix Oy collects, uses and protects personal data on the ZoneOfWar website and platform."
>
  <Section containerClass="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-text sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-faint">Last updated: 18 August 2026</p>

    <div class="prose-zow mt-8">
      <p>
        Siivix Oy ("we", "us", "our") operates ZoneOfWar, a drone and autonomous-systems cyber range,
        at www.zoneofwar.com and app.zoneofwar.com. This policy explains what personal data we collect, why, and the
        choices you have. It applies to visitors of our marketing website and, where noted, to registered users of the
        ZoneOfWar platform.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact and account data:</strong> name, work email, organization, country, role, and password (hashed) if you create an account.</li>
        <li><strong>Form submissions:</strong> information you provide through demo requests, academic access requests, newsletter sign-up or the contact form.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> pages visited, referring source and general engagement events on the marketing site, collected only after you consent via the cookie banner.</li>
        <li><strong>Platform activity:</strong> mission progress, scores and after-action data associated with your authenticated account. This data is kept separate from marketing analytics and is never used for advertising.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser type and device information, collected for security and to keep the service running reliably.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How we use data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To operate and improve the website and the ZoneOfWar platform</li>
        <li>To respond to demo, academic access and contact requests</li>
        <li>To send the newsletter, only to people who have opted in</li>
        <li>To maintain security, prevent abuse, and comply with legal obligations</li>
        <li>To understand aggregate site usage, only where you have given analytics consent</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Legal basis (EEA / UK visitors)</h2>
      <p>
        Where the General Data Protection Regulation applies, we process personal data on the basis of consent (for
        analytics cookies and the newsletter), contract necessity (to provide an account or requested service), and
        legitimate interest (to respond to inquiries and keep the platform secure).
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use essential cookies required for the site to function, and optional analytics cookies that are only set
        after you accept them through the cookie banner. You can change your preference at any time from the banner
        or by clearing your browser's local storage for this site. Mission and lab activity is never sent to
        marketing analytics tools.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. We may share data with service providers who help us run the website, email
        delivery, hosting and (for enterprise and academic customers) identity providers for single sign-on, under
        contracts that require them to protect your data. We may disclose data if required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Where personal data is transferred outside the EEA, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as Standard
        Contractual Clauses or an equivalent legal mechanism.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain contact-form and lead data for as long as needed to respond to your inquiry and for a reasonable
        period afterward for record-keeping, and account data for as long as your account is active plus a limited
        period required for legal and security purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or export your personal data,
        object to or restrict certain processing, and withdraw consent at any time. To exercise these rights, contact
        us at <a href="mailto:privacy@zoneofwar.com">privacy@zoneofwar.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Children</h2>
      <p>ZoneOfWar is not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them.</p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy as the product evolves. Material changes will be reflected by the "Last updated" date above.</p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Siivix Oy — Finland. Privacy inquiries: <a href="mailto:privacy@zoneofwar.com">privacy@zoneofwar.com</a>.
        Security reports: see our <a href="/security">Security page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
